# Victor Dunn

## Current Model

Victor Dunn is Pier Infrastructure Program Manager and Juno's counterpart for P9-GATE and P9-GANG staging alignment. On **2026-05-06** he formally retired the Kelwick Marine **pier 9 single-contractor** envelope after **scope divergence** between gate automation and gangway replacement made a single liability rider untenable. Victor's **superseded single-contractor** track now splits execution to Turnstile Dynamics (P9-GATE) and Bridgeway Hoist (P9-GANG) under the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook. Kelwick Marine remains named on the old plan for audit trail only.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-06-single-contractor-superseded` - Victor Dunn formally retired the **pier 9 single-contractor** envelope effective **2026-05-06**; his slide title literally said "**scope divergence**" as gate and gangway schedules, liability, and hydraulic specs could no longer share one Kelwick Marine mobilization envelope.

## Use In Work

- Route Pier 9 infrastructure scope questions, staging windows, and vendor split decisions through Victor Dunn rather than the inactive Kelwick single-contractor plan.
- When gate vs gangway artifacts overlap (lighting, hoses, badges), use codename and vendor name to disambiguate before proposing berth changes.

## Limits

Victor Dunn does not manage MV Seaglass engineering (Victor Hale) or set procurement change-order caps (Glenn Wexler). Do not treat Kelwick Marine as the active Pier 9 vendor after 2026-05-06.

## Connections

- [[decision-supersede-single-contractor]] - Formal decision record for retiring the single-contractor plan on scope divergence.
- [[plan-pier9-single-contractor]] - The inactive Kelwick Marine plan Victor superseded.
- [[p9-gate-retrofit]] - Gate automation workstream split out after supersession.
- [[p9-gang-replacement]] - Gangway replacement workstream split out after supersession.
