# P9-Gate Retrofit

## Current Model

The **Pier-9 Gate Retrofit** project tracks under codename **P9-GATE** and covers fare lane automation, gate automation, and night lighting circuit upgrades at Pier 9. Introduced at Q2 kickoff still under the Kelwick single-contractor envelope, the **gate retrofit** scope split to Turnstile Dynamics after Victor Dunn superseded unified contracting on 2026-05-06. Victor Dunn's **p9-gate redesign** mock-up review on 2026-05-01 confirmed **4 lanes** after redesign review — each **fare gate lane** width matches the playbook passenger flow table with no fifth-lane squeeze. Gangway staging on P9-GANG remains on a separate calendar.

## Evidence

- `2026-04-20-q2-kickoff-terminal` - Week-1 kickoff introduces **Pier-9 Gate Retrofit** as **P9-GATE** (fare lanes, Turnstile-adjacent scope) rolling up under Victor Dunn's Pier 9 Single-Contractor Plan with Kelwick Marine as vendor of record.
- `2026-04-24-pier9-dual-scope-intro` - Victor Dunn splits whiteboard columns for **Pier-9 Gate Retrofit** (four preliminary fare lanes, gate automation, night lighting) vs gangway work; **P9-GATE** codename goes live in the terminal readiness playbook tracker.
- `2026-05-01-gate-lane-redesign` - Victor Dunn confirms **p9-gate redesign** mock-up holds **4 lanes** after redesign review with no fifth-lane squeeze; Juno verifies each **fare gate lane** width against the playbook passenger flow table.

## Use In Work

- Disambiguate Pier 9 artifacts by codename P9-GATE and component (fare gate lane count, night lighting) rather than generic "pier 9 retrofit" language shared with P9-GANG.
- Hold gate lane layout to four fare lanes per the redesign mock-up unless Victor Dunn and Turnstile Dynamics reopen the squeeze review.

## Limits

P9-GATE does not own gangway hydraulic hose specs (SAE 100R2AT on P9-GANG) or Bridgeway Hoist delivery dates. Gate delivery later slipped to 2026-05-28, separate from gangway May 21 hold.

## Connections

- [[p9-gang-replacement]] - Adjacent Pier 9 workstream sharing staging vocabulary but separate codename and vendor.
- [[victor-dunn]] - Infrastructure program manager who confirmed lane redesign and split vendor tracks.
- [[turnstile-dynamics]] - P9-GATE gate automation vendor after procurement split.
